  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Workshop Series - United States-Southeast Asia Aviation Cooperation Program Workshop Series Phase II, through Futron Corporation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">USTDA funding would support a series of four (4) workshops to provide a broad range of managerial, technical, safety, efficiency, capacity, and operational training to key officials from civil aviation authorities, airlines, air navigation providers, and/or individual airport operators in Southeast Asia and Pacific Islands. The U.S.-Southeast Asia Aviation Cooperation Program Workshops Series Phase II would serve as a forum where representatives from U.S. industry and government engage Southeast Asian and Pacific Island counterparts to collaborate on best practices, standards, and policy development for the regions aviation industry.</narrative>
  </description>
